# AMBER's GTP torsion terms, tabulated, one record per four-atom
# quadruplet enumerated from the topology in amber_tabulate_gtp.py.
#
# No installed AMBER force field defines GTP: the types are AMBER's own
# guanosine types for every shared atom, and for the nine extra ones the
# type of the role they play -- P for the phosphorus, O2 for a
# non-bridging oxygen, OS for a bridging ester. The four P-O-P torsions
# therefore resolve through AMBER's generic phosphoester wildcard
# X -OS-P -X, 1.046 kJ/mol at periodicity 3, which is the approximation
# this file declares. CHARMM36's own published GTP puts the same term at
# 0.544 kJ/mol; it was read as a magnitude check and not used.
#
# TORSIONTABLE <id> <bins> <E_0> <T_0> ... over phi in [-180, 180]
# TORSION <res> <FAMILY> <a1> <a2> <a3> <a4> <table>
# STIFFNESS <res> <a1> <a2> <k>   k in kJ.mol-1.A-2
